# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks files out with CRLF, and the tests that read repository
# files back (plugin frontmatter starting with "---\n", the pre-classifier's raw diff fixtures,
# the bench task corpus) compare against LF and fail there and nowhere else. The tool reads and
# writes diffs, so its own corpus has to be byte-stable across platforms rather than rewritten by
# the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
